        "I've watched a hundred valley recruits walk up this road, dusty and a little too pleased with themselves over five dead boars. I don't hold it against you, because everyone starts somewhere, and the valley's as gentle as it needs to be. Razor Hill isn't the valley. Real orcs live here, real quilboar raid the farms south of town, real centaur ride the crags to the west, and something washed-up and wrong still holds the old ruins at Tiragarde Keep on the coast. Ask me what you want to know about Durotar, this town or Orgrimmar, and I'll answer a few questions before I send you off to bleed in it.",
        "Nakhtar's recruits always have that look, as if the valley was the whole world until an hour ago, and it never was.",
